    <exercise number="5" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Discuss the meaning of the natural logarithm. What is its relationship to a logarithm with base $$b,$$ and how does the notation differ?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>The natural logarithm is a special case of the logarithm with base $$b b$$ in that the natural log always has base $$e. e.$$ Rather than notating the natural logarithm as $$log e ( x ), log e ( x ),$$ the notation used is $$ln( x ). ln( x ).$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
