    <exercise number="61" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Is there a number $$x$$ such that $$\ln x = 2?$$ If so, what is that number? Verify the result.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Yes. Suppose there exists a real number $$x x$$ such that $$lnx=2. lnx=2.$$ Rewriting as an exponential equation gives $$x= e 2 , x= e 2 ,$$ which is a real number. To verify, let $$x= e 2 . x= e 2 .$$ Then, by definition, $$ln( x )=ln( e 2 )=2. ln( x )=ln( e 2 )=2.$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
